    "result_text": "There's only one test class, and it passes. The full build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `checkDigit` field to the owner response: a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`.\n\nChanges kept structural impact low by adding a small, cohesive unit rather than growing any existing method or class:\n\n1. **`util/CheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny, single-purpose class with one static `luhn(String)` method, mirroring the existing util pattern (`CustomerCode`, `Locality`, `IdentityKey`). It has no surrounding complexity to hold.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating to `CheckDigit.luhn(owner.getCustomerCode())`, exactly matching the existing derived-field mappings. The mapper method body is unchanged (MapStruct-generated), so no method's complexity grew.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` schema property (int32, 0\u20139) so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode`, which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit, passes \u2014 and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
